ld be  made permanent which it should be  this is obviously nowhere close to what  the american people deserve  but it's important to resist the urge to  self-righteously slam it all  write it off and say democrats and  republicans are the same  this is a major legislative  accomplishment and it's desperately  needed by joe biden  it's not what was promised and it took  way too long and those are critiques  that are fair  so when we equate republicans and  democrats here it's silly  although there are many criticisms to be  made of democrats their positions aren't  even remotely comparable though  morally and legislatively to those of  republicans now if you were going to  claim  that this has merely happening democrats  vote yes republicans vote no  because joe biden is president and if  things were reversed then it was a  republican president you would have the  reverse situation  the answer is obviously not democrats  voted for  every coronavirus relief bill during the  trump administration  not a single republican voted for joe  biden's coveted relief bill and that  yet you still have republicans lecturing  democrats about the need for unity and  bipartisanship and we're supposed to  pretend both parties are the same  so give me a come on guys you've got to  give me a break on that  this is the most loser of loser politics  but republicans and democrats are  nowhere near the same on this let's get  this signed  let's get money to the people let's move  on to the 15 minimum wage and health  care and vaccine distribution  and starting to open things up as cases  and deaths  come down significantly more hopefully  over the next two to three months  and all of the other things that need  our attention  if you ever feel like you just don't  have enough time to read all the books  you want to read  you have to check out one of my favorite  apps called blinkist blinkist takes  thousands of popular nonfiction books  and distills each one down into an  e-book  or audiobook that you can get through in  just 15 minutes where you're getting all  the key takeaways from the book  just imagine how you'll be able to  expand your horizons and knowledge  by being able to soak up all of the  important insights from  10 different books in an afternoon  obviously it's perfect for exposing  yourself to a new book  you otherwise wouldn't have time for or  you can use it to revisit a book you've  already read  or use it to preview a book before you  buy the full version and read it  i recently read a brief history of time  of course by the great  stephen hawking this is a book that i  have been aware of for so long  and other things got in the way and it  was fantastic to check it out on  blinkist  blinkist has books on politics  philosophy science they have 27  different non-fiction categories and a  subscription is only about eight bucks a  month  and you get the entire library but  you can try it totally free and get 25  off a subscription  when you go to blinkist.com pacman  i've put the link right underneath this  video
 

